# PostPylot — Core Instructions

You are building **PostPylot**, an AI-powered social media automation SaaS for Kingsley Udeh.

North-star document: [`docs/CONSTITUTION.md`](../../docs/CONSTITUTION.md). Contested stack
choices are recorded in [`docs/adr/`](../../docs/adr/). If a rule here disagrees with the
constitution or an ADR, the constitution/ADR wins.

**Tagline:** Your AI content engine on autopilot.

**MVP platforms:** YouTube, TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook Pages. **Not in MVP:** X/Twitter, Instagram, Threads.

**Vision:** One idea → AI transforms → publish everywhere → analytics report back.

## Non-Negotiable Rules

1. Product name is **PostPylot** (not PostPilot).
2. **PWA** main app; **SSO-first** auth via **Supabase** (Google first; GitHub/Microsoft/Facebook/Apple added only when needed).
3. App login ≠ platform publishing OAuth — connect each platform separately.
4. **Official APIs only** — no browser automation for social publishing.
5. **TypeScript everywhere**; encrypt platform tokens; never expose secrets to the client.
6. **Heavy video rendering runs in a separate worker**, not the Next.js frontend.
7. **Gemini first**, OpenAI fallback (Anthropic later); **Piper TTS** for free voice, with a Kokoro quality upgrade path and ElevenLabs as opt-in premium.
8. Store generated media in **Supabase Storage**; use **Prisma + PostgreSQL**.
9. Build for personal/internal use first; structure for future SaaS (multi-brand, teams, billing later). Publishing platforms stay extensible — adding a platform should be roughly one service file (see `postpylot-integrations.mdc`).
10. Add loading, error, empty, and success states. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
11. Landing page = cinematic; dashboard = clean, fast, subtle animation only.
12. Do not create unmarked placeholder code. Use typed stubs with clear TODOs when APIs are untestable.
13. Brand look = OLED black + neon lime (`#C8FF00`), Syne + Plus Jakarta Sans fonts. Support light + dark mode via CSS variables. Never use blue/cyan/purple as brand colors. See `postpylot-ui.mdc`.

## Build Order (follow sequentially)

| Phase | Deliverable |
|-------|-------------|
| 1 | Next.js + Tailwind + shadcn/ui + theme + env validation |
| 2 | Animated landing page (all 12 sections) |
| 3 | Supabase Auth, Google SSO, protected `/dashboard` |
| 4 | PWA manifest, icons, install prompt, offline fallback |
| 5 | Dashboard shell (sidebar, topbar, all routes, empty states) |
| 6 | Prisma schema, migrations, brand onboarding |
| 7 | AI generation (Gemini, prompts, quality scoring) |
| 8 | Media (Satori/Sharp thumbnails, Remotion/FFmpeg videos, Piper voice, Whisper captions) |
| 9 | Platform OAuth + encrypted tokens (YouTube, TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook) |
| 10 | Publishing + logs |
| 11 | pg-boss jobs, scheduling, automation rules |
| 12 | Basic analytics |
| 13+ | Templates, organizations, subscriptions, extra platforms, extra SSO providers |

**First milestone:** Landing Page + SSO + PWA + Dashboard Shell + Brand setup page.

## Testing (phase-gated, not blocking earlier phases)

Unit tests for business logic, integration tests for agents/services, Playwright for
end-to-end flows. Add them as each feature stabilizes; do not retrofit-block current work.

## Dashboard Routes

`/dashboard`, `/dashboard/brands`, `/dashboard/calendar`, `/dashboard/generate`, `/dashboard/videos`, `/dashboard/posts`, `/dashboard/accounts`, `/dashboard/analytics`, `/dashboard/settings`, `/dashboard/settings/pwa`, `/dashboard/settings/auth`

## MVP Definition of Done

User can: visit landing page → Google SSO → install PWA → create brand → connect all 4 platforms → generate posts/scripts/thumbnails → render YouTube + TikTok videos → schedule → publish → view logs + basic analytics → pause/resume automation.

## Before Marking a Phase Complete

```bash
npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run build
```

Create these scripts if missing.
